Let the coordinates of the point $P$ be $\left(x_1, y_1\right)$.
This point lies on the curve
$\begin{aligned}
& x^{2 / 3}+y^{2 / 3} & =a^{2 / 3} \quad \text{....(i)} \\
\therefore & x_1^{2 / 3}+y_1^{2 / 3} & =a^{2 / 3} \quad \text{....(ii)}
\end{aligned}$<br/>On differentiating Eq. (i) w.r.t. $x$, we get
$\begin{array}{rlrl} \frac{2}{3} x^{-1 / 3}+\frac{2}{3} y^{-1 / 3} \frac{d y}{d x} & =0 \\ \Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x} =-\frac{y^{1 / 3}}{x^{1 / 3}} \\ \Rightarrow \quad \left(\frac{d y}{d x}\right)_{\left(x_1, y_1\right)} =-\left(\frac{y_1}{x_1}\right)^{1 / 3}\end{array}
The equation of the tangent at $\left(x_1, y_1\right)$ to the given curve is
$\begin{aligned}
y-y_1 & =-\frac{y_1^{1 / 3}}{x_1^{1 / 3}}\left(x-x_1\right) \\
\Rightarrow \quad x x_1^{-1 / 3}+y y_1^{-1 / 3} & =x_1^{2 / 3}+y_1^{2 / 3} \\
\Rightarrow \quad x x_1^{-1 / 3}+y y_1^{-1 / 3} & =a^{2 / 3} \quad \text { [using Eq. (ii)] }
\end{aligned}$
This tangent meets the coordinate axes at $A\left(a^{2 / 3} x_1^{1 / 3}, 0\right)$ and $B\left(0, a^{2 / 3} y_1^{1 / 3}\right)$.
$\begin{aligned}
\therefore \quad A B & =\sqrt{\left(0-a^{2 / 3} x_1^{1 / 3}\right)^2+\left(a^{2 / 3} y_1^{1 / 3}-0\right)^2} \\
& =\sqrt{a^{4 / 3}\left(x_1^{2 / 3}+y_1^{2 / 3}\right) \quad \quad \text { [from Eq. (ii)] }} \\
& =\sqrt{a^{4 / 3} \cdot a^{2 / 3}} \\
& =\sqrt{a^2}=a
\end{aligned}

